---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const UPDATED = '21 October 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Trutech Business collects, uses and protects personal information.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" lead={`Last updated ${UPDATED}`} />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose legal-text">
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal information {site.brand} (“we”, “us”) collects when you use this website
        or work with us, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We handle personal information in line with
        Ghana’s Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843).
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.brand} is a technology and design business based in {site.location}. You can reach us at
        {site.email && <> <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></>}
        {site.phone && <> or {site.phone}</>}.
      </p>

      <h2>Browsing this website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The website has no user accounts, advertising or analytics trackers, and it doesn’t set cookies.</li>
        <li>If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your own browser only.</li>
        <li>
          Like any website, the services that deliver it receive technical information such as your IP address and
          browser type: GitHub Pages (hosting), Google Fonts (fonts) and Supabase (portfolio content and images).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When you contact us</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form doesn’t store anything on this website. It opens WhatsApp or your email app with your
        message ready to send, so we receive only what you choose to send: usually your name, contact details and
        project details. WhatsApp and your email provider handle your message under their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>When you’re our client</h2>
      <p>To deliver and review your work, we keep:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, and your WhatsApp number if you give it to us;</li>
        <li>the project title, our messages to you and the files we prepare for you;</li>
        <li>the feedback, approvals and ratings you send through your private link;</li>
        <li>when your private link was first opened.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is stored with Supabase, our database and file storage provider, on servers in London,
        United Kingdom. Your files can only be opened through your private link, which we can switch off, replace or
        set to expire, and only the {site.brand} administrator can manage them.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to reply to you and prepare quotes;</li>
        <li>to deliver, review and support the work you asked for;</li>
        <li>to keep business records such as approvals and payments;</li>
        <li>to show completed work in our portfolio, as described in our <a href={`${base}terms/`}>Terms</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don’t sell personal information or use it for advertising.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Only the service providers that run this website and our work: Supabase (database and files), GitHub
        (website hosting), Google Fonts (fonts) and WhatsApp or email when you use them to talk to us. We may also
        share information when the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep client files for as long as we need them to deliver and support your project, usually up to 12 months
        after delivery, then delete them. We keep approvals, reviews and payment records as business records. You can
        ask us to delete your information sooner.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, to correct it, or to delete it, and you can
        withdraw any consent you gave. Contact us using the details above. If you’re not satisfied with our answer,
        you can complain to the Data Protection Commission of Ghana.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are for businesses, schools and adults. Work for schools is arranged with the school, not with
        students directly.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we’ll update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal-text {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .legal-text h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.8rem);
    margin-top: 1.8em;
  }
  .legal-text li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
